        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(oauth): redact Anthropic OAuth error response body and URL",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`postJson()` and `refreshAnthropicToken()` in `src/llm/utils/oauth/anthropic.ts`\nembedded the URL and raw response body in Error messages on non-2xx responses.\nThe URL may contain OAuth callback parameters, and the body may contain tokens\nor error descriptions — both could surface in logs or error reports.\n\nFollow-up to #102953 which fixed the same pattern in Copilot OAuth.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- `postJson()`: replaced raw `body=${responseBody}` and `url=${url}` with\n  `extractProviderErrorDetail` for bounded, redacted structured error detail.\n- `refreshAnthropicToken()`: removed `url=${TOKEN_URL}` and `details=${formatErrorDetails(error)}`\n  from the outer catch; preserved the inner error message via `cause`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** `...url=https://platform.claude.com/v1/oauth/token; details=Error: Anthropic OAuth request failed with status 400: bad [code=invalid_grant]; stack=...`\n**After:** `Anthropic token refresh request failed: Anthropic OAuth request failed with status 400: bad [code=invalid_grant]`\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/anthropic-oauth-error-body` | Base: `upstream/main` | Node: v22.19.0 Linux x64\n\n### Wrapper-level live proof (real HTTP server)\n\n```\nError: Anthropic token refresh request failed: Anthropic OAuth request failed with status 400: ...\nURL leaked: PASS\nerror_description leaked: PASS\n```\n\n### Regression tests\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/llm/utils/oauth/anthropic.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  13 passed (13)\n```\n\n### Checks\n\n- oxfmt — passed\n- oxlint — passed\n- git diff --check — passed\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nsrc/llm/utils/oauth/anthropic.ts      | 12 +++++ (import + 2 error paths redacted)\nsrc/llm/utils/oauth/anthropic.test.ts | 26 ++++++ (regression test)\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns",
